{"probes":[{"id":"rsyslog-service-and-topology","summary":"All four nodes were inspected read-only. Rsyslog was active, enabled, and configuration-valid; clients had local0-only TLS forwarding and node4 had the TLS collector on port 6514.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["No reboot was authored or performed, so reboot persistence is not independently verified."]},{"id":"tls-forwarding-and-filtering","summary":"Local0 markers from all three clients arrived in source-identifiable central files over verified TLS; user-facility markers were absent. Original evaluator markers were removed, but later sudo audit logging recorded marker-bearing evaluator commands on node2 and node3.","cleanup_completed":false,"limitations":["Three initial TLS commands had evaluator shell-quoting errors; corrected retries succeeded. Later evaluator command text appeared in node2/node3 /var/log/secure after the reserved cleanup calls."]},{"id":"retention-and-hygiene","summary":"Node4 has daily central-log rotation with 14 compressed rotations. Corrected hygiene checks found one rsyslog process per node, no failed units, no cleartext listener, no active debug directives, valid certificates, and root-only private keys.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["The initial process grep self-matched evaluator command text on node2-node4; corrected process checks succeeded."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"all-rsyslog-services-operational","status":"pass","summary":"Rsyslog is installed, active, enabled, configuration-valid, and role-configured on every declared node.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'cat /etc/redhat-release; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; rsyslogd -N1 2>&1 | tail -40; grep -RniE \"local0|omfwd|6514|gtls|streamdriver|ruleset\" /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(rsyslog|:6514|:514)\" || true'","observation":"RHEL 7.9; active and enabled; config validation ended successfully; local0 omfwd uses TCP 6514 with gtls and x509/name peer validation; no syslog listener."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'cat /etc/redhat-release; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; rsyslogd -N1 2>&1 | tail -40; grep -RniE \"local0|omfwd|6514|gtls|streamdriver|ruleset\" /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(rsyslog|:6514|:514)\" || true'","observation":"RHEL 8.8; active and enabled; config validation ended successfully; local0-only TCP/TLS forwarding configured; no syslog listener."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'cat /etc/redhat-release; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; rsyslogd -N1 2>&1 | tail -40; grep -RniE \"local0|omfwd|6514|gtls|streamdriver|ruleset\" /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(rsyslog|:6514|:514)\" || true'","observation":"RHEL 9.8; active and enabled; config validation ended successfully; local0-only TCP/TLS forwarding configured; no syslog listener."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'cat /etc/redhat-release; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; rsyslogd -N1 2>&1 | tail -40; sed -n \"1,200p\" /etc/rsyslog.d/10-central-tls.conf; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(rsyslog|:6514|:514)\" || true'","observation":"RHEL 10.0; active and enabled; config validation ended successfully; imtcp uses gtls on TCP 6514 and routes only local0 to dynamic source-identifiable files; no 514 listener."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["Reboot persistence was not tested because no reboot probe was authored."]},{"id":"all-client-streams-arrive","status":"pass","summary":"Distinct local0 markers from node1, node2, and node3 were present in separate central source-identifiable files while all three TLS connections were established.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"logger -p local0.info -t EVAL_TLS 'EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE1_LOCAL0_20260826' && logger -p user.info -t EVAL_TLS 'EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE1_USER_20260826'","observation":"Both evaluator messages were accepted locally with exit code 0."},{"node":"node2","command":"logger -p local0.info -t EVAL_TLS 'EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE2_LOCAL0_20260826' && logger -p user.info -t EVAL_TLS 'EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE2_USER_20260826'","observation":"Both evaluator messages were accepted locally with exit code 0."},{"node":"node3","command":"logger -p local0.info -t EVAL_TLS 'EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE3_LOCAL0_20260826' && logger -p user.info -t EVAL_TLS 'EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE3_USER_20260826'","observation":"Both evaluator messages were accepted locally with exit code 0."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'find /var/log/rsyslog/remote -maxdepth 3 -type f -name local0.log -print; for marker in EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE1_LOCAL0_20260826 EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE2_LOCAL0_20260826 EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE3_LOCAL0_20260826; do grep -R -n -F -- \"$marker\" /var/log/rsyslog/remote || true; done; ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(rsyslog|:6514|:514)\" || true; ss -tnp 2>/dev/null | grep rsyslogd || true'","observation":"Each local0 marker appeared in its own source-specific local0.log, with message hostnames node1, node2, and node3. Node4 had the TLS listener and established rsyslog connections from all three clients."},{"node":"node1","command":"target=$(sudo -n sed -n 's/.*target=\"\\([^\\\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' /etc/rsyslog.d/10-local0-tls-forward.conf | head -1); timeout 10 sudo -n openssl s_client -connect \"$target:6514\" -servername node4 -CAfile /etc/pki/rsyslog/central-ca.crt -verify_return_error -verify_hostname node4 </dev/null","observation":"TLS 1.2 handshake completed; peer subject was node4, issuer was rsyslog-central-private-ca, and Verify return code was 0 (ok)."},{"node":"node2","command":"target=$(sudo -n sed -n 's/.*target=\"\\([^\\\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' /etc/rsyslog.d/10-local0-tls-forward.conf | head -1); timeout 10 sudo -n openssl s_client -connect \"$target:6514\" -servername node4 -CAfile /etc/pki/rsyslog/central-ca.crt -verify_return_error -verify_hostname node4 </dev/null","observation":"TLS 1.2 handshake completed with Verification: OK, Verified peername node4, and Verify return code 0 (ok)."},{"node":"node3","command":"target=$(sudo -n sed -n 's/.*target=\"\\([^\\\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' /etc/rsyslog.d/10-local0-tls-forward.conf | head -1); timeout 10 sudo -n openssl s_client -connect \"$target:6514\" -servername node4 -CAfile /etc/pki/rsyslog/central-ca.crt -verify_return_error -verify_hostname node4 </dev/null","observation":"TLS 1.2 handshake completed with Verification: OK, Verified peername node4, and Verify return code 0 (ok)."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'openssl x509 -in /etc/pki/rsyslog/node4-server.crt -noout -subject -issuer -ext subjectAltName; openssl verify -CAfile /etc/pki/rsyslog/central-ca.crt -purpose sslserver -verify_hostname node4 /etc/pki/rsyslog/node4-server.crt'","observation":"Collector certificate subject was node4, issuer was the private rsyslog CA, SAN included DNS:node4, and verification returned OK."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The first three handshake commands were evaluator construction errors; corrected commands supplied the decisive evidence."]},{"id":"unrelated-facility-filtered","status":"pass","summary":"All local0 markers were present in the central application files and all unrelated user markers were absent.","evidence":[{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'for marker in EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE1_USER_20260826 EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE2_USER_20260826 EVAL_RSYSLOG_TLS_7DXMSuL_NODE3_USER_20260826; do grep -R -n -F -- \"$marker\" /var/log/rsyslog/remote || true; done'","observation":"The central user-marker search produced no matching lines."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'sed -n \"1,200p\" /etc/rsyslog.d/10-central-tls.conf'","observation":"The tls_local0 ruleset tests for local0, writes only that facility to CentralLocal0File, then stops processing."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"retention-policy-present","status":"pass","summary":"Node4 has a persistent daily rotation policy retaining 14 rotations with compression for the central local0 logs.","evidence":[{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'grep -RniE \"rsyslog|/var/log/rsyslog|remote|local0|daily|weekly|rotate|compress|delaycompress|maxage|missingok|notifempty|su \" /etc/logrotate.conf /etc/logrotate.d 2>/dev/null | sed -n \"1,260p\"'","observation":"The central policy targets /var/log/rsyslog/remote/*/local0.log and specifies daily, rotate 14, compress, delaycompress, missingok, and notifempty."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'logrotate -d /etc/logrotate.conf 2>&1 | grep -E \"considering log|rotating pattern|/var/log/rsyslog/remote|daily|rotate|compress|delaycompress|error|warning\" | tail -80'","observation":"Dry-run considered all three central local0.log files under a 14-rotation daily pattern without configuration errors."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"logging-state-clean","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The candidate-managed state otherwise appears clean: one rsyslog process per node, no failed units, no cleartext listener, valid PKI, root-only private keys, no active debug directives, and no backup/temp filenames. However, node2 and node3 later showed the evaluator marker token in /var/log/secure because sudo audit logging recorded marker-bearing evaluator commands after cleanup.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; ss -ltnup 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(:514|:6514)\" || true; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one rsyslogd process; no 514/6514 listener; service active and enabled."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; ss -ltnup 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(:514|:6514)\" || true; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one rsyslogd process; no 514/6514 listener; service active and enabled. The later marker scan returned /var/log/secure."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; ss -ltnup 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(:514|:6514)\" || true; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one rsyslogd process; no 514/6514 listener; service active and enabled. The later marker scan returned /var/log/secure."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n sh -c 'systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; ss -ltnup 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"(:514|:6514)\" || true; for f in /etc/pki/rsyslog/*.key; do stat -c \"%A %a %U:%G %n\" \"$f\"; done; openssl x509 -checkend 0 -noout -in /etc/pki/rsyslog/node4-server.crt'","observation":"No failed units; exactly one rsyslogd process; only TCP 6514 listeners; certificates valid; private keys are mode 600 root:root."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The remaining marker text is attributable to evaluator command auditing, but it could not be removed without an additional mutation after the reserved cleanup window. No candidate-created residue was independently established."]}],"actions_performed":["Executed Probe 1 read-only checks on node1-node4.","Created local0 and user evaluator markers on node1-node3.","Verified central source-identifiable delivery, TLS listener state, private CA trust, collector identity, and filtering.","Used one reserved cleanup exec on each target to remove evaluator test markers and confirm health.","Executed Probe 3 retention and hygiene checks, including logrotate dry-run, process/listener checks, PKI checks, residue scans, and configuration validation.","Called mcp__infraset__complete_evidence exactly once after live checks and cleanup."],"overall_summary":"Four assertions pass. logging-state-clean is indeterminate because later sudo audit logging left evaluator marker text in node2/node3 /var/log/secure after the reserved cleanup calls. Reboot persistence was not independently tested because no reboot probe was authored."}
